# Local
.DS_Store
.env

# Secrets — never commit. site_config.json is the important one: a Frappe
# site's config holds the database credentials AND the encryption key that
# decrypts every stored password on the site. The rest are the files an
# operator is most likely to create next to a checkout while following
# deploy/README.md — deploy/.env.example tells them to write `kamra.env`.
site_config.json
.env.*
!.env.example
kamra.env
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
.npmrc
.pypirc
secrets.json

# Internal operator plans — keep local only, never publish
PLAN.md
docs/adr-str.md
docs-site/node_modules/
docs-site/.vitepress/dist/
docs-site/.vitepress/cache/

graphify-out/
node_modules

# Build artifact: the Windows installer is a release asset, attached to a
# GitHub Release rather than committed. Rebuild it with:
#   makensis deploy/windows/ZiriPms-Setup.nsi
deploy/windows/*.exe
